{"id":"mahabharata-13-042","work":"mahabharata","part":13,"partName":"अनुशासनपर्व","partNameEn":"Anushasana Parva","unit":42,"title":"द्विचत्वारिंशत्तमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 42 · Vipula is sent for flowers","summary":{"en":"Vipula, proud of his austerity, goes through penance after obeying his guru, and Devasharma later sends him for flowers. On the way he meets a couple who, quarrelling over a task, call on those who are guilty of sin, and he realises that he himself has done the sin of the guru's wife by taking her body.","kn":"ವಿಪುಲ ಗುರುವಿನ ಮಾತಿನಂತೆ ತಪಸ್ಸು ಮಾಡಿ ತನ್ನ ತಪಸ್ಸಿನ ಬಗ್ಗೆ ಹೆಮ್ಮೆಪಡುತ್ತಾನೆ; ದೇವಶರ್ಮ ಅವನನ್ನು ಹೂವಿಗೆ ಕಳುಹಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ. ದಾರಿಯಲ್ಲಿ ಜಗಳವಾಡುವ ದಂಪತಿ ಪಾಪಿಗಳ ಹೆಸರು ಹೇಳುವುದನ್ನು ಕೇಳಿ ತಾನೂ ಗುರುಪತ್ನಿಯ ದೇಹ ಪ್ರವೇಶಿಸಿ ಪಾಪ ಮಾಡಿದೆನೆಂದು ಅರಿಯುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"विपुल गुरु की आज्ञा के बाद तप करके अपने तप पर गर्व करने लगता है, और देवशर्मा उसे फूल लाने भेजते हैं। मार्ग में झगड़ते दम्पति को पापियों का नाम लेते सुनकर वह समझता है कि गुरुपत्नी के शरीर में प्रवेश कर उसने भी दोष किया।","te":"విపులుడు గురువు మాట ప్రకారం తపస్సు చేసి తన తపస్సుకు గర్వపడతాడు; దేవశర్మ అతన్ని పూల కోసం పంపుతాడు. దారిలో గొడవపడే దంపతులు పాపుల పేర్లు చెప్పడం విని గురుపత్ని శరీరంలో ప్రవేశించి తానూ పాపం చేశానని గ్రహిస్తాడు.","ta":"விபுலன் குருவின் சொல்படி தவம் செய்து தன் தவத்தில் பெருமை கொள்ள, தேவசர்மா அவனைப் பூக்களுக்கு அனுப்புகிறார். வழியில் சண்டையிடும் தம்பதியர் பாவிகளின் பெயர்களைக் கூறுவதைக் கேட்டு, குருபத்தினியின் உடலில் புகுந்ததால் தானும் பாவம் செய்தேன் என்று உணர்கிறான்.","ml":"തപസ്സിൽ അഭിമാനിക്കുന്ന വിപുലൻ ഗുരുവിന്റെ കല്പന അനുസരിച്ച് തപസ്സു ചെയ്തശേഷം, ദേവശർമ്മ പിന്നീട് അദ്ദേഹത്തെ പൂക്കൾ കൊണ്ടുവരാൻ അയയ്ക്കുന്നു. വഴിയിൽ ജോലിയെച്ചൊല്ലി തർക്കിക്കുന്ന ഒരു ദമ്പതികളെ കാണുന്നു; അവർ പാപം ചെയ്തവരെ വിളിച്ചുപറയുന്നു. ഗുരുപത്നിയുടെ ശരീരത്തിൽ പ്രവേശിച്ചതിലൂടെ താനും ഗുരുപത്നിയുടെ പാപം ചെയ്തുവെന്ന് അദ്ദേഹം തിരിച്ചറിയുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 13.42; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Nov 03 2026","sections":[{"title":"आनुशासनिकपर्व","titleEn":"Anushasanika Parva (The instructions)","verses":[{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"विपुलस्त्वकरोत्तीव्रं तपः कृत्वा गुरोर्वचः ।\nतपोयुक्तमथात्मानममन्यत च वीर्यवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Vipula, having carried out his teacher's word, practiced intense austerity, and the mighty man came to think of himself as rich in austerity."}},{"n":2,"text":"स तेन कर्मणा स्पर्धन्पृथिवीं पृथिवीपते ।\nचचार गतभीः प्रीतो लब्धकीर्तिर्वरो नृषु ॥","meaning":{"en":"Lord of the earth, vying with the earth through that deed, he roamed fearless and glad, famed and foremost among men."}},{"n":3,"text":"उभौ लोकौ जितौ चापि तथैवामन्यत प्रभुः ।\nकर्मणा तेन कौरव्य तपसा विपुलेन च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Descendant of Kuru, the master also thought that he had won both worlds by that deed and by his great austerity."}},{"n":4,"text":"अथ काले व्यतिक्रान्ते कस्मिंश्चित्कुरुनन्दन ।\nरुच्या भगिन्या दानं वै बभूव धनधान्यवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, after some time had passed, delight of the Kurus, a gift of wealth and grain came to Ruchi's sister."}},{"n":5,"text":"एतस्मिन्नेव काले तु दिव्या काचिद्वराङ्गना ।\nबिभ्रती परमं रूपं जगामाथ विहायसा ॥","meaning":{"en":"At that very time a certain divine and lovely woman of surpassing beauty passed through the sky."}},{"n":6,"text":"तस्याः शरीरात्पुष्पाणि पतितानि महीतले ।\nतस्याश्रमस्याविदूरे दिव्यगन्धानि भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Flowers of divine fragrance fell from her body to the ground not far from his hermitage, Bharata."}},{"n":7,"text":"तान्यगृह्णात्ततो राजन्रुचिर्नलिनलोचना ।\nतदा निमन्त्रकस्तस्या अङ्गेभ्यः क्षिप्रमागमत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Lotus-eyed Ruchi picked them up, king. Then an invitation quickly came for her from her sister's side."}},{"n":8,"text":"तस्या हि भगिनी तात ज्येष्ठा नाम्ना प्रभावती ।\nभार्या चित्ररथस्याथ बभूवाङ्गेश्वरस्य वै ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dear son, her elder sister was named Prabhavati, and she was the wife of Chitraratha, king of the Angas."}},{"n":9,"text":"पिनह्य तानि पुष्पाणि केशेषु वरवर्णिनी ।\nआमन्त्रिता ततोऽगच्छद्रुचिरङ्गपतेर्गृहान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The fair-complexioned Ruchi put those flowers in her hair and, being invited, went to the house of the king of the Angas."}},{"n":10,"text":"पुष्पाणि तानि दृष्ट्वाथ तदाङ्गेन्द्रवराङ्गना ।\nभगिनीं चोदयामास पुष्पार्थे चारुलोचना ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing those flowers, the lovely-eyed wife of the Anga king urged her sister to get her flowers like them."}},{"n":11,"text":"सा भर्त्रे सर्वमाचष्ट रुचिः सुरुचिरानना ।\nभगिन्या भाषितं सर्वमृषिस्तच्चाभ्यनन्दत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Fair-faced Ruchi told her husband everything her sister had said, and the sage approved of it."}},{"n":12,"text":"ततो विपुलमानाय्य देवशर्मा महातपाः ।\nपुष्पार्थे चोदयामास गच्छ गच्छेति भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the great ascetic Devasharma called Vipula and urged him, Bharata, saying: Go, go, for the flowers."}},{"n":13,"text":"विपुलस्तु गुरोर्वाक्यमविचार्य महातपाः ।\nस तथेत्यब्रवीद्राजंस्तं च देशं जगाम ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Without a second thought, the great ascetic Vipula said, So be it, king, and went to that place."}},{"n":14,"text":"यस्मिन्देशे तु तान्यासन्पतितानि नभस्तलात् ।\nअम्लानान्यपि तत्रासन्कुसुमान्यपराण्यपि ॥","meaning":{"en":"In the place where the flowers had fallen from the sky there were still others that had not wilted."}},{"n":15,"text":"ततः स तानि जग्राह दिव्यानि रुचिराणि च ।\nप्राप्तानि स्वेन तपसा दिव्यगन्धानि भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"He took those divine and lovely flowers of heavenly fragrance, Bharata, which he had obtained by his own austerity."}},{"n":16,"text":"संप्राप्य तानि प्रीतात्मा गुरोर्वचनकारकः ।\nततो जगाम तूर्णं च चम्पां चम्पकमालिनीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Gladdened at obtaining them and doing his teacher's word, he then went swiftly to Champa, garlanded with champaka trees."}},{"n":17,"text":"स वने विजने तात ददर्श मिथुनं नृणाम् ।\nचक्रवत्परिवर्तन्तं गृहीत्वा पाणिना करम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"In a lonely forest, dear son, he saw a man and a woman, holding each other's hand, going round and round like a wheel."}},{"n":18,"text":"तत्रैकस्तूर्णमगमत्तत्पदे परिवर्तयन् ।\nएकस्तु न तथा राजंश्चक्रतुः कलहं ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"One of them hurried along, turning in the same footprints; the other, king, did not go so fast, and so the two quarreled."}},{"n":19,"text":"त्वं शीघ्रं गच्छसीत्येकोऽब्रवीन्नेति तथापरः ।\nनेति नेति च तौ तात परस्परमथोचतुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"One said, You go too fast, and the other said, No. They said to each other again and again, No, no, dear son."}},{"n":20,"text":"तयोर्विस्पर्धतोरेवं शपथोऽयमभूत्तदा ।\nमनसोद्दिश्य विपुलं ततो वाक्यमथोचतुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As they contended so, they swore an oath, and thinking of Vipula in their minds, they then said:"}},{"n":21,"text":"आवयोरनृतं प्राह यस्तस्याथ द्विजस्य वै ।\nविपुलस्य परे लोके या गतिः सा भवेदिति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whichever of us has told an untruth, let him go to the fate in the next world that the brahmin Vipula goes to."}},{"n":22,"text":"एतच्छ्रुत्वा तु विपुलो विषण्णवदनोऽभवत् ।\nएवं तीव्रतपाश्चाहं कष्टश्चायं परिग्रहः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing this, Vipula became downcast. He thought: I have practiced such severe austerity, and this burden I carry is painful."}},{"n":23,"text":"मिथुनस्यास्य किं मे स्यात्कृतं पापं यतो गतिः ।\nअनिष्टा सर्वभूतानां कीर्तितानेन मेऽद्य वै ॥","meaning":{"en":"What sin have I committed that this couple has named for me, before all beings, a fate that no one would want?"}},{"n":24,"text":"एवं संचिन्तयन्नेव विपुलो राजसत्तम ।\nअवाङ्मुखो न्यस्तशिरा दध्यौ दुष्कृतमात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thinking thus, best of kings, Vipula lowered his face and head and reflected on his own wrongdoing."}},{"n":25,"text":"ततः षडन्यान्पुरुषानक्षैः काञ्चनराजतैः ।\nअपश्यद्दीव्यमानान्वै लोभहर्षान्वितांस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then he saw six other men playing dice with gold and silver pieces, full of greed and joy."}},{"n":26,"text":"कुर्वतः शपथं तं वै यः कृतो मिथुनेन वै ।\nविपुलं वै समुद्दिश्य तेऽपि वाक्यमथाब्रुवन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"While making an oath like the couple's one, they too spoke words aimed at Vipula."}},{"n":27,"text":"यो लोभमास्थायास्माकं विषमं कर्तुमुत्सहेत् ।\nविपुलस्य परे लोके या गतिस्तामवाप्नुयात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whoever among us, giving in to greed, would dare to cheat, let him go to the fate in the next world that Vipula goes to."}},{"n":28,"text":"एतच्छ्रुत्वा तु विपुलो नापश्यद्धर्मसंकरम् ।\nजन्मप्रभृति कौरव्य कृतपूर्वमथात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing this, Vipula could find no mixing of dharma in anything he had done from his birth onward, descendant of Kuru."}},{"n":29,"text":"स प्रदध्यौ तदा राजन्नग्नावग्निरिवाहितः ।\nदह्यमानेन मनसा शापं श्रुत्वा तथाविधम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, king, hearing such a curse, he brooded, his mind burning like a fire fed with fire."}},{"n":30,"text":"तस्य चिन्तयतस्तात बह्व्यो दिननिशा ययुः ।\nइदमासीन्मनसि च रुच्या रक्षणकारितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As he brooded, dear son, many days and nights passed, and it came to his mind that he had guarded Ruchi in that way."}},{"n":31,"text":"लक्षणं लक्षणेनैव वदनं वदनेन च ।\nविधाय न मया चोक्तं सत्यमेतद्गुरोस्तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Putting his marks against her marks and his face against her face, I did not tell my teacher this truth at that time."}},{"n":32,"text":"एतदात्मनि कौरव्य दुष्कृतं विपुलस्तदा ।\nअमन्यत महाभाग तथा तच्च न संशयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Descendant of Kuru, Vipula then considered this a misdeed in himself, greatly blessed one, and so it undoubtedly was."}},{"n":33,"text":"स चम्पां नगरीमेत्य पुष्पाणि गुरवे ददौ ।\nपूजयामास च गुरुं विधिवत्स गुरुप्रियः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Reaching the city of Champa, he gave the flowers to his teacher and, as one dear to his teacher, duly honored him."}}]}]}